# Michael - traditionele spiritual ("Michael, row the boat ashore")
# Traditioneel; voor het eerst opgetekend tijdens de Amerikaanse Burgeroorlog op
# St. Helena Island (Sea Islands, South Carolina), gedrukt in Slave Songs of the
# United States (1867) (Wikipedia, en; SecondHandSongs). Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit MICHAEL.ROW (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Akkoorden alleen boven het
# eerste couplet, geplaatst naar de kolommen van de bron; Nederlandse notatie (F#mi,
# Gmi) als F#m en Gm geschreven. Het akkoord "A1" in de bron is gelezen als A7.
# De bron geeft een andere versie van het derde couplet; die staat als laatste.
{title: Michael}
{subtitle: Michael, row the boat ashore}
{meta: id michael}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit MICHAEL.ROW (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Wikipedia (en) en SecondHandSongs}
{meta: tag geestelijk}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Michael [A7]row the boat [D]ashore, [D7]Hal[G]lelu[D]jah
[F#m]Michael row the boat [G6]a[Gm]shore, [D]Halle[A7]lu[D]jah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Sister help to trim the sail, Hallelujah
Sister help to trim the sail, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Jordan river is deep and wide, Hallelujah
Meet my Mother on the other side, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The river is deep and the river is wide, Hallelujah
Milk and honey in the other side, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The river Jordan is chilly and cold, Hallelujah
Chills the body not the soul, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Then you'll hear the trumpet sound, Hallelujah.
Then you'll hear the trumpet sound, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Trumpet sound the world around, Hallelujah.
Trumpet sound the world around, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Trumpet sound the jubilee, Hallelujah.
Trumpet sound the jubilee, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Trumpet sound for you and me, Hallelujah.
Trumpet sound for you and me, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Gabriel blows the trumpet horn, Hallelujah.
Gabriel blows the trumpet horn, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Michael's boat is a gospelboat, Hallelujah.
Michael's boat is a gospelboat, Hallelujah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Michael's boat is a music boat, Hallelujah
Michael's boat is a music boat, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Andere versie van het derde couplet}

{start_of_verse}
The river is deep and the river is wide, Hallelujah
Green pastures on the other side, Hallelujah
{end_of_verse}
